import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Methodology" description="How evidence is sourced, graded and disclosed on LongevityStack." current="methodology" canonicalPath="/methodology/">
  <main class="ls-shell">
    <article style="max-width: 68ch; padding: 64px 0 96px;" class="ls-article">
      <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 600; font-size: 46px; letter-spacing: -0.015em; margin: 0 0 28px;">Methodology</h1>
      <h2>Sourcing</h2>
      <p>Primary sources only — peer-reviewed trials and meta-analyses, read directly, not summarised secondhand. Every claim carries a citation with a PMID where one exists.</p>
      <h2>The strength indicator</h2>
      <p>Each evidence block on this site carries a five-step strength bar. It weighs study design (meta-analysis and RCT outrank observational data), sample size, and whether the finding has been independently replicated. It is a judgment call, made transparently, not an algorithm — disagreement is welcome via the "Report an error" link on every article.</p>
      <h2>What "reviewed" means</h2>
      <p>Every reference page carries a "last reviewed" date in its header. That is the date the sources were last re-checked against current literature — not the publish date. Pages due for re-review are not silently left stale.</p>
      <h2>Disclosure</h2>
      <p>Affiliate links are marked inline, next to the recommendation, not in a footer nobody reads. See the full <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
